It is worth analyzing the implementation of the method that passes all changes applied to
DBContext to the database:
public async Task<bool> SaveEntitiesAsync()
{
try
{
return await SaveChangesAsync() > 0;
}
catch (DbUpdateConcurrencyException ex)
{
foreach (var entry in ex.Entries)
{
entry.State = EntityState.Detached;
}
throw ex;
}
}
The preceding implementation just calls the SaveChangesAsync DBContext
context method that saves all changes to the database, but then it intercepts all concurrency
exceptions and detaches from the context all entities involved in the concurrency error. This
way, next time a command retries the whole failed operation, their updated versions will
be reloaded from the database.
